The run exposes a methodological subtlety: the framework's `REGIME_STABLE` verdict depends on the *null's* dispersion, which itself shifts under cost (the coin-flip null trades ~2/3 of bars vs the candidate's ~100%), so verdict-based classification is confounded. I'll make the primary classification depend on the candidate's own net-of-cost medians, keeping the framework verdict as secondary context.
