+## CORRECTION — momentum / mean-reversion signal defect (campaign slot 02, task R-001, run 43476207596)
+
+While running the contracted cost-sensitivity check for lookback 3/5/10
+momentum, a **verified implementation defect** was found in the signal
+functions that produced the prior momentum/reversal evidence. This section
+supersedes the interpretation (not the raw figures) of the momentum and
+mean-reversion results recorded above.
+
+### The defect
+
+`research/backtest/regime_stability.py`:
+
+- `momentum_signals(closes, lookback)` computes
+  `ret = mean(log(closes[i-lookback+1 : i+1]))` — the mean log **PRICE**
+  over the window — and sets `weight = +1 if ret > 0 else -1`. For every
+  collected large-cap (adjusted close > 1) this is always positive, so the
+  signal is a **constant LONG on every bar**, independent of the lookback.
+  It does **not** implement "long the previous lookback-day return".
+- `mean_reversion_signals(closes, lookback)` has the same defect with the
+  opposite sign and is a **constant SHORT**.
+
+Empirical confirmation (this activation): for AAPL/AMZN/JPM/XOM,
+`momentum_signals` emits weight +1 on 4460/4460 non-neutral bars (0 short)
+at lookbacks 3/5/10; `mean_reversion_signals` emits weight -1 on all
+non-neutral bars; a corrected return-based momentum signal
+(`log(close[i]) - log(close[i-lookback])`) flips ~800-900 times over ~4.5k
+bars. The prior artifacts' identical medians across lookbacks 3/5/10 are the
+signature of this degeneracy (the signal is identical at every lookback).
+
+### Consequences for prior conclusions (recorded, not deleted)
+
+- The **momentum SUPPORTED (7/10 REGIME_STABLE)** verdict describes a
+  constant-long equity-beta / drift bet, **not a momentum anomaly**. It is
+  evidence of positive large-cap drift over 2009-2026, not of short-horizon
+  return autocorrelation.
+- The **reversal FALSIFIED** verdict describes a constant-short (which loses
+  in a rising market); it does not test the reversal hypothesis.
+- The reported **-0.99 momentum/reversal P&L correlation** is trivially -1
+  (constant +1 vs constant -1).
+- The **lookback 3/5/10 robustness** (`momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json`)
+  and the **longer-horizon (20/60) robustness** (`momentum_longer_horizon.py`,
+  also uses `bt.momentum_signals`) are **vacuous**: the signal is identical at
+  every lookback, so the "robustness" is a tautology.
+- The per-asset **momentum/reversal evidence base is invalid pending re-test**
+  with a repaired signal.
+
+Not affected by this defect: `breakout_signals` (price-level comparison) and
+`cs_momentum_spread_daily_returns` (uses `log(c[i]) - log(c[i-lookback])`),
+so the breakout and cross-sectional-momentum results stand on their own
+implementation.
+
+### Cost-sensitivity result (contracted deliverable)
+
+Bounded cost grid {zero, realistic, 2x, 4x} x the repository's existing
+realistic cost model (`commission_per_trade=2.0`, `commission_per_share=0.003`,
+`slippage_cents=2.0`, `slippage_proportional=0.0005`), lookbacks 3/5/10, each
+level vs a matched coin-flip null, on the 10-asset collected universe.
+Artifact: `state/check_artifacts/momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json`.
+Independent verifier: `research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py`
+(all four gates MATCH).
+
+Cost-robustness classification (primary rule: verdict in
+{REGIME_STABLE, REGIME_DEPENDENT} and all per-segment net-of-cost medians > 0;
+COST_ROBUST = edge at zero+realistic+4x):
+
+- **existing (constant-long) candidate:** COST_ROBUST = 7 (AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL,
+  AMZN, META, TSLA, JPM); NO_EDGE_AT_ZERO_COST = 3 (NVDA, JNJ, XOM). The
+  classification is **identical at lookbacks 3, 5 and 10** — the degeneracy
+  signature. Per-segment medians (~+0.05..+0.13) are essentially unchanged from
+  zero to 4x cost because the position is low turnover (3.81x annualized on
+  AMZN; $21,055 realistic commission vs $284,746 for the corrected signal). It
+  is cost-robust **because it is beta, not because momentum survives costs**.
+- **corrected return-based momentum diagnostic:** NO_EDGE_AT_ZERO_COST = 10/10
+  at every lookback. There is no robust short-horizon momentum edge to survive
+  cost stress; where marginally positive (e.g. AAPL) it erodes under cost, and
+  the signal is ~105x turnover.
+
+### Answer to the primary question
+
+The short-horizon momentum edge does **not** survive conservative cost stress,
+because — as implemented and as corrected — there is **no robust short-horizon
+momentum edge** on this universe. The prior positive evidence is an artifact of
+the signal defect. This is durable negative/reframing evidence, independently
+recomputed and deterministic.
+
+### Next
+
+Repair `momentum_signals` / `mean_reversion_signals` to use the previous
+lookback-day return, add unit tests, and re-run the momentum and mean-reversion
+cells (including the cost grid) through the full gate stack with a fresh
+independent verifier. See `agent_02.json` candidate task R-002.
+
